🌐 Computer Networking Notes
🔹 1. Network
✅ Definition
A network is a group of interconnected devices (computers, phones, servers) that communicate and share resources.
💡 Meaning
Devices = nodes
Communication = data transfer
Medium = wired (cables) or wireless (Wi-Fi)
🔸 Types of Network
Type.   Meaning.                    Example
LAN    Local Area Network       School lab
MAN  Metropolitan Area Network  City network
WAN. Wide Area Network.         Internet
PAN. Personal Area Network.Bluetooth devices
🔹 2. IP Address
✅ Definition
An IP address is a unique identifier assigned to each device on a network.
🔸 Types (Host & Network Part)
An IP address has 2 parts:
Network Part → identifies the network
Host Part → identifies the device
Example:
192.168.1.10
Network = 192.168.1
Host = 10
🔸 IP Classes (IPv4)
Class.   Range.      Use
A.      1 – 126.    Large networks
B.      128 – 191.  Medium
C.      192 – 223.  Small
D.      224 – 239.  Multicast
E.      240 – 255   Experimental
🔸 IPv4 vs IPv6
Feature.    IPv4.        IPv6
Format.     32-bit.      128-bit
Example.    192.168.1.1  2001:db8::1
Size.       Limited.     Very large
Security.   Basic.       Better
🔹 3. TCP vs UDP
🔸 TCP (Transmission Control Protocol)
Reliable
Connection-oriented
Slow but accurate
Example: Web, Email
🔸 UDP (User Datagram Protocol)
Fast ⚡
No connection
Less reliable
Example: Streaming, Games
🔹 4. MAC Address
✅ Definition
A MAC address is a physical (hardware) address assigned to a network interface card.
💡 Key Points
Unique for each device
Works in Data Link Layer
Example: 00:1A:2B:3C:4D:5E
